- op: discuss  # b01b
  at: '2026-07-28T09:08:06Z'  # b01b
  by: agent  # b01b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b01b
  clock: 4  # b01b
  nonce: b01b  # b01b
  message: "PR #50 (dev b8d6e3f8c9): fixed. DataModel gains a rank_score field separating the centrality ranking signal from confidence (ADR-0039 ruling 3). detect_datamodels no longer mutates confidence with the centrality boost (which conflated detection reliability with importance and via min(1.0,...) could reach the reserved 1.0 ceiling); rank_score = confidence + boost, and both the detection ordering and the sketch data-model rendering sort by rank_score (confidence stats still sum confidence). Evidence: test_centrality_boosts_rank_score_not_confidence (confidence stays the 0.95 seed, rank_score>0.95>confidence) + test_to_dict (rank_score serialized); full affected slice green, 100% cov. No schema change (DataModel is not a schema-validated output; generate-schema --check clean). Mirrors the Edge/entrypoint confidence/rank_score split."  # b01b
